elivery Network (CDN) authorization with AWS Elemental MediaPackage to help protect your content from unauthorized use. When CDN authentication is configured, it prevents users from bypassing the CDN in order to directly access content on the origin.\n\nAWS offers the most purpose-built services for direct-to-consumer (D2C) and streaming to help companies reliably deliver, monetize, and support live and on-demand media over the internet, and bring unparalleled experiences to screens everywhere. Explore https://aws.amazon.com/media/direct-to-consumer-d2c-streaming/ to learn more.\n\nFind more AWS for Media & Entertainment Video Tutorials here","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/media/aws-for-me-video-tutorials-cdn-authorization-for-aws-elemental-mediapackage/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Class: Aws::MediaPackageVod::Types::UpdatePackagingGroupResponse\n \n — AWS SDK for Ruby V2","context":"## Instance Attribute Details\n\n### #**arn** ⇒ String\n\nReturns:\n\n* (String)\n\n### #**authorization** ⇒ Types::Authorization\")\n\nCDN Authorization credentials\n\nReturns:\n\n* (Types::Authorization\"))\n —\n\n CDN Authorization credentials.\n\n### #**domain_name** ⇒ String\n\nReturns:\n\n* (String)\n\n### #**id** ⇒ String\n\nReturns:\n\n* (String)\n\n### #**tags** ⇒ Hash<String,String>\n\nA collection of tags associated with a resource\n\nReturns:\n\n* (Hash<String,String>)\n —\n\n A collection of tags associated with a resource.\n\nGenerated on Fri Feb 21 17:35:22 2025 by\nyard\n0.9.34 (ruby-2.7.8)","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-ruby/v2/api/Aws/MediaPackageVod/Types/UpdatePackagingGroupResponse.html"}]}}

